# CHANGE 1: REMOVE the existing SMTP_* env vars from the `backend`
# service environment block (SMTP_HOST, SMTP_PORT, SMTP_USER,
# SMTP_PASSWORD, SMTP_FROM_EMAIL, SMTP_FROM_NAME).
#
# CHANGE 2: ADD these three vars to the `backend` service
# environment block:

      SENDGRID_API_KEY: ${SENDGRID_API_KEY:-}
      SENDGRID_FROM_EMAIL: ${SENDGRID_FROM_EMAIL:-}
      SENDGRID_FROM_NAME: ${SENDGRID_FROM_NAME:-MarketEye}

# CHANGE 3: Do the SAME removal + addition in the `celery_worker`
# service environment block. Celery sends alert emails through the
# same notification_service.send_email() path, so it needs the
# SendGrid credentials too.
#
# CHANGE 4: Confirm FRONTEND_BASE_URL is already wired in the
# `backend` service (it should be). If not, add:
#
#       FRONTEND_BASE_URL: ${FRONTEND_BASE_URL:-https://app.yourdomain.com}
